%% DM26-0670

%% The runtime side, as built (2026-11-04, docs/architecture/signed-configuration.md, "How it fits together"), read against polar-scheduler and polar-agent-builder/src/signed.rs.
%% The shaded step is designed and not built: the observer verifies nothing today. The target verifies regardless.
%% An agent that has just registered asks for what is held for it: general/configuration_replay.
sequenceDiagram
    participant Server as Polar git server
    participant Cassini
    participant Sync as Scheduler observer<br/>(git sync)
    participant Watch as Scheduler observer<br/>(watcher)
    participant Processor as Scheduler processor
    participant Target as Target agent
    participant CA as ConfigurationActor<br/>(in the target)
    participant Graph as Neo4j

    autonumber
    Server-)Cassini: RepoChanged, after an accepted push
    Cassini-)Sync: RepoChanged (for its repository)
    Sync->>Server: git pull --ff-only (mTLS, workload certificate)
    Note over Sync: It also pulls on its interval, and a failed pull waits for the next
    Sync-->>Watch: the checkout changed, seen by the file watcher
    Watch->>Watch: evaluate the .dhall under permanent, adhoc or ephemeral to JSON, imports off:<br/>a file with an import is refused, and what it names is not read. Hold the rest for replay

    rect rgb(235, 219, 178)
    Note over Watch: DESIGNED (signed-configuration.md), not built
    Watch->>Watch: verify with the target's rules, drop and log if invalid
    end

    Watch-)Cassini: GitScheduleChange { path, whole document } on the scheduler's topic
    Cassini-)Processor: GitScheduleChange
    Processor->>Graph: write a Configuration node, document as received
    alt its version is above the last this processor forwarded for that id
        Processor-)Cassini: ConfigurationNotification on agent.NAME.configuration
        Cassini-)Target: ConfigurationNotification (every agent subscribes to its own)
        Target->>CA: Deliver(document)
    else not newer, or no agent can be read from it
        Note over Processor,Graph: Recorded and not forwarded. One that cannot be routed is written as unroutable, with why
    end

    Note over Target,CA: verifies for itself, in order, stopping at the first failure
    CA->>CA: 1. two fields only
    CA->>CA: 2. chain to pinned CA, cert valid, may sign,<br/>signature over the payload
    CA->>CA: 3. only now read the payload:<br/>its shape, by its type
    CA->>CA: 4. addressed to this agent
    CA->>CA: 5. signer may make this change: Cedar first,<br/>the signer's capability where none speaks.<br/>A section made of policy: its capability only
    CA->>CA: 6. the signer's certificate is not revoked<br/>(the authority's revoked serials)
    CA->>CA: 7. version above the last: the document's,<br/>or for a runtime section, that section's
    alt a configuration document passes
        CA->>CA: apply the Dynamic variables: all or none
        opt a value changed
            CA-)Target: ConfigChanged { version, changed }
            Target->>CA: current() and use the new values
        end
        CA->>CA: record names, never values
    else a runtime document passes
        CA->>CA: judge the body (the section's rule, and the<br/>agent's judge if it has one), replace it whole
        CA-)Target: RuntimeChanged { section, version }
    else any check fails
        CA->>CA: refuse whole, keep old values.<br/>A refused body does not spend its version
    end
    Note over CA,Processor: Either way it says what it did: applied, unchanged, stale, invalid or unverified
    CA-)Cassini: ConfigurationOutcome (status and why, no value)
    Cassini-)Processor: ConfigurationOutcome, with who the broker says published it
    Processor->>Graph: write an outcome node, linked to the item
